      "dcDescription": [
        "East Africa Eritrea Hold with a toil. from the Afar people. \n\nThe dagger has a leaf of iron and a handle made of wood decorated with a brass knife. The vagina is made of leather and is also decorated with a brass bud as an extension of the tip. A leather strap is wrapped around the vagina, it is probably to be attached to life. \n\nThe dagger is derived from the Afare people in the Aseb, according to the catalogue. The local name given is “gooddess.”(HTB) North East Africa 1907.42.0475 Östafrika Eritrea Dolk med slida. från afarfolket. \n\nDolken har ett blad av järn och ett handtag av trä dekorer"
